Index,SS / Module,Feature,Test Case Name,Test Description,Speed,Mode,Memory Start Offset,Memory End Offset,Remarks,Test Steps / Procedure,Impacted Registers,Validation / Acceptance Criteria,Code Generation (Required / Not),Hidden_Test_Case_Name,Hidden_Test_Description,Hidden_Remarks,Hidden_Test_Steps_Procedure,Hidden_Impacted_Registers,Hidden_Validation_Acceptance_Criteria
1,GPIO,Negative edge interrupt enable (neie),test_gpio_nedge_walking_zeros_pattern,"Validate negative-edge interrupt behavior across GPIO pads using a walking-zero stimulus while pads are configured in input mode with group interrupts enabled. The ISR verifies per-pad DIN and raw status, group status set/clear, and system raw status clear.",NA,ISR,0xA0243ffc,0xA0243ffc,NA,"1) Enable INTR_EN1 for the selected GPIO instance.
2) Program gp0_intr2_intr_en1 for pads to input mode with negative-edge interrupt enabled.
3) Configure GPIO_IO_CTRL_GROUP1, GPIO_IO_CTRL_GROUP2, GPIO_IO_CTRL_GROUP3, and gpio_io_ctrl_group4 for input mode.
4) Enable group interrupts by writing to INTR1_INTR_EN1.
5) Apply a walking-zero stimulus to generate a falling edge per pad and wait for the handler to complete.
6) In the handler, read the per-pad control register to check DIN and raw interrupt status; read INTR1_INTR_STS1 for the group bit.
7) Clear the per-pad interrupt via the per-pad control register and verify the cleared state.
8) Verify group interrupt status clears in INTR1_INTR_STS1 and clear the system raw status in RAW_STCR1.","INTR_EN1, INTR1_INTR_EN1, INTR1_INTR_STS1, RAW_STCR1, GPIO_IO_CTRL_GROUP1, GPIO_IO_CTRL_GROUP2, GPIO_IO_CTRL_GROUP3, gpio_io_ctrl_group4, gp0_intr2_intr_en1","1) DIN status after the falling edge indicates expected input level → Pass when input status reflects the expected level.
2) Per-pad raw interrupt status indicates a negative-edge event → Pass when the raw status is set for the pad.
3) Group interrupt status bit is set for the pad → Pass when the corresponding bit is set in INTR1_INTR_STS1.
4) After clearing, the per-pad control readback matches the cleared state → Pass when the readback equals the expected clear pattern.
5) Group interrupt status becomes zero after clear → Pass when INTR1_INTR_STS1 reads zero.
6) System raw status is cleared → Pass when RAW_STCR1 shows the corresponding bit cleared.",,"test_gpio_nedge_walking_zeros_pattern","Enable sysreg interrupts for GPIO0 or GPIO1. For i=0..31, write 0x00040000 to MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8 + (i*4) to enable negative-edge interrupt. Configure input mode for all pads by writing 0x000000FF to MIZAR_GPIO_GPIO_IO_CTRL_GROUP1/2/3/4. Enable group interrupts by writing 0xFFFFFFFF to MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_INTR1_INTR_EN1. For each i=0..31: set wr_val = 1<<i, write 0xFFFFFFFF to 0xA0243ffc, then write ~(wr_val) to 0xA0243ffc to generate a falling edge, set int_pend=1 and wait until ISR clears it. In Default_IRQHandler: set int_pend=0; write 0xFFFFFFFF to 0xA0243ffc; read rdata from MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8 + (i*4); if (rdata & 0x1) != 0 then DIN check passes else print error and increment test_err; if (rdata & 0x2) != 0 then read rdata_grp from MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_INTR1_INTR_STS1 and check (1<<i) bit else print \"Interrupt Not occured\" and increment test_err; clear per-pad interrupt by writing 0x00110001 to MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8 + (i*4), read back and verify 0x100001 else increment test_err; read MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_INTR1_INTR_STS1 and verify 0x0 else increment test_err; clear system raw status by writing LSS_SYSREG_RAW_STCR1_GPIO0_INTR or LSS_SYSREG_RAW_STCR1_GPIO1_INTR to MIZAR_LSS_SYSREG_RAW_STCR1 and verify bit cleared; finally clear GIC IRQ 87/88 as applicable; finish(test_err).",NA,"1) If GPIO0 is defined, GIC_EnableIRQ(87); if GPIO1 is defined, GIC_EnableIRQ(88). 2) test_err = 0. 3) If GPIO0 is defined, write_reg(MIZAR_LSS_SYSREG_INTR_EN1, LSS_SYSREG_INTR_EN1_GPIO0_INTR); if GPIO1 is defined, write_reg(MIZAR_LSS_SYSREG_INTR_EN1, LSS_SYSREG_INTR_EN1_GPIO1_INTR). 4) For i=0..31: write_reg(MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8 + (i*4), 0x00040000). 5) wait_on(10). 6) write_reg(MIZAR_GPIO_GPIO_IO_CTRL_GROUP1, 0x000000FF); write_reg(MIZAR_GPIO_GPIO_IO_CTRL_GROUP2, 0x000000FF); write_reg(MIZAR_GPIO_GPIO_IO_CTRL_GROUP3, 0x000000FF); write_reg(MIZAR_GPIO_GPIO_IO_CTRL_GROUP4, 0x000000FF); wait_on(10). 7) write_reg(MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_INTR1_INTR_EN1, 0xFFFFFFFF). 8) For i=0..31: wr_val = 1<<i; write_reg(0xA0243ffc, 0xFFFFFFFF); wait_on(30); write_reg(0xA0243ffc, ~(wr_val)); wait_on(30); int_pend=1; while(int_pend==1) { print \"Waiting for interrupt\"; wait_on(10); }. 9) finish(test_err). ISR: wr_val = 1<<i; int_pend=0; write_reg(0xA0243ffc, 0xFFFFFFFF); rdata = read_reg(MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8 + (i*4)); if((rdata & 0x1) != 0) pass else print error and test_err++; if((rdata & 0x2) != 0) { rdata_grp=read_reg(MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_INTR1_INTR_STS1); if((rdata_grp & (1<<i)) != 0) pass else print error and test_err++; write_reg(MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8 + (i*4), 0x00110001); wait_on(2); rdata = read_reg(MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8 + (i*4)); if(rdata == 0x100001) pass else print error and test_err++; rdata_grp = read_reg(MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_INTR1_INTR_STS1); if(rdata_grp == 0x0) pass else print error and test_err++; if GPIO0 defined: write_reg(MIZAR_LSS_SYSREG_RAW_STCR1, LSS_SYSREG_RAW_STCR1_GPIO0_INTR); read back and ensure bit cleared; if GPIO1 defined: write_reg(MIZAR_LSS_SYSREG_RAW_STCR1, LSS_SYSREG_RAW_STCR1_GPIO1_INTR); read back and ensure bit cleared; } else { print \"Interrupt Not occured\"; test_err++; } If GPIO0: GIC_ClearIRQ(87); If GPIO1: GIC_ClearIRQ(88).","MIZAR_LSS_SYSREG_INTR_EN1, LSS_SYSREG_INTR_EN1_GPIO0_INTR, LSS_SYSREG_INTR_EN1_GPIO1_INTR, MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8, MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_INTR1_INTR_EN1, MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_INTR1_INTR_STS1, MIZAR_LSS_SYSREG_RAW_STCR1, LSS_SYSREG_RAW_STCR1_GPIO0_INTR, LSS_SYSREG_RAW_STCR1_GPIO1_INTR","- In ISR: if ((rdata & 0x1) != 0) then pass for DIN check; else print error and increment test_err.
- In ISR: if ((rdata & 0x2) != 0) then raw interrupt detected; else print \"Interrupt Not occured\" and increment test_err.
- Group status: rdata_grp = read_reg(MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_INTR1_INTR_STS1); if ((rdata_grp & (1<<i)) != 0) then pass; else print error and increment test_err.
- After clear sequence: rdata from per-pad register must equal 0x100001; if equal then pass; else print error and increment test_err.
- Group status clear: rdata_grp must equal 0x0; if equal then pass; else print error and increment test_err.
- System raw status clear (GPIO0 path): after write to MIZAR_LSS_SYSREG_RAW_STCR1 with LSS_SYSREG_RAW_STCR1_GPIO0_INTR, readback & LSS_SYSREG_RAW_STCR1_GPIO0_INTR must be 0; if 0 then pass; else print error and increment test_err.
- System raw status clear (GPIO1 path): after write to MIZAR_LSS_SYSREG_RAW_STCR1 with LSS_SYSREG_RAW_STCR1_GPIO1_INTR, readback & LSS_SYSREG_RAW_STCR1_GPIO1_INTR must be 0; if 0 then pass; else print error and increment test_err." 
1,GPIO,Negative edge interrupt enable (neie),test_gpio_negedge_intr_en,"Configure GPIO pads for input with negative-edge interrupts and verify per-pad and group interrupt behavior. The handler confirms status, clears interrupts, and validates system status clear.",NA,ISR,0xA0243ffc,0xA0243ffc,NA,"1) Enable INTR_EN1 for the applicable GPIO instance.
2) For each pad, program gp0_intr2_intr_en1 to input mode with negative-edge interrupt enabled.
3) Enable the corresponding bit in INTR1_INTR_EN1 for the active pad.
4) Drive the stimulus to create a falling edge via the memory-mapped interface and wait for the handler to complete.
5) In the handler, read the per-pad control register to check DIN and raw interrupt status and read INTR1_INTR_STS1 for the group bit.
6) Clear the per-pad interrupt by writing the clear pattern to the per-pad control register and verify the readback.
7) Verify the group interrupt status in INTR1_INTR_STS1 is cleared.
8) Clear the system raw status in RAW_STCR1 for the GPIO instance.","INTR_EN1, INTR1_INTR_EN1, INTR1_INTR_STS1, RAW_STCR1, gp0_intr2_intr_en1","1) DIN indicates the expected input level after the event → Pass when the input status shows the expected level.
2) Per-pad raw interrupt status indicates a negative-edge event → Pass when the raw status is set for the pad.
3) Group interrupt status bit is set for the active pad → Pass when the corresponding bit is set in INTR1_INTR_STS1.
4) After clearing, the per-pad control readback matches the cleared state → Pass when the readback equals the expected clear pattern.
5) Group interrupt status reads zero after clear → Pass when INTR1_INTR_STS1 is zero.
6) System raw status is cleared → Pass when RAW_STCR1 shows the corresponding bit cleared.",,"test_gpio_negedge_intr_en","Enable sysreg interrupt for GPIO0 or GPIO1. Initialize test_err = 0. Write 0xFFFFFFFF to 0xA0243ffc. For i = 0..31: set addr1 = MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8 + (i*4); write_reg(addr1, 0x00140000) to configure input mode and enable negative-edge interrupt; wait_on(50); wr_val = 1<<i; enable group interrupt by write_reg(MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_INTR1_INTR_EN1, wr_val); wait_on(10); write_reg(0xA0243ffc, 0xFFFFFFFF); wait_on(30); write_reg(0xA0243ffc, ~(wr_val)); set int_pend = 1; while(int_pend) wait_on(10). In Default_IRQHandler: set int_pend = 0; write_reg(0xA0243ffc, 0xFFFFFFFF); raddr = MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8 + (i*4); rdata = read_reg(raddr); if((rdata & 0x1) != 0x0) pass else test_err++; if((rdata & 0x2) != 0x0) { rdata_grp = read_reg(MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_INTR1_INTR_STS1); if((rdata_grp & wr_val) != 0) pass else test_err++; raddr2 = MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8 + (i*4); write_reg(raddr2, 0x00110001); rdata = read_reg(raddr2); if(rdata == 0x100001) pass else test_err++; rdata_grp = read_reg(MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_INTR1_INTR_STS1); if(rdata_grp == 0x0) pass else test_err++; clear system raw status by writing LSS_SYSREG_RAW_STCR1_GPIO0_INTR or LSS_SYSREG_RAW_STCR1_GPIO1_INTR to MIZAR_LSS_SYSREG_RAW_STCR1; clear GIC IRQ 87/88 } else { test_err++; } finish(test_err).",NA,"1) If GPIO0 defined: GIC_EnableIRQ(87); if GPIO1 defined: GIC_EnableIRQ(88). 2) test_err = 0. 3) If GPIO0 defined: write_reg(MIZAR_LSS_SYSREG_INTR_EN1, LSS_SYSREG_INTR_EN1_GPIO0_INTR); if GPIO1 defined: write_reg(MIZAR_LSS_SYSREG_INTR_EN1, LSS_SYSREG_INTR_EN1_GPIO1_INTR). 4) write_reg(0xA0243ffc, 0xFFFFFFFF). 5) For i=0..31: addr1 = MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8 + (i*4); write_reg(addr1, 0x00140000); wait_on(50); wr_val = 1<<i; write_reg(MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_INTR1_INTR_EN1, wr_val); wait_on(10); write_reg(0xA0243ffc, 0xFFFFFFFF); wait_on(30); write_reg(0xA0243ffc, ~(wr_val)); int_pend = 1; while(int_pend) { wait_on(10); }. 6) finish(test_err). ISR: int_pend = 0; write_reg(0xA0243ffc, 0xFFFFFFFF); raddr = MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8 + (i*4); rdata = read_reg(raddr); if((rdata & 0x1) != 0x0) pass else test_err++; if((rdata & 0x2) != 0x0) { rdata_grp = read_reg(MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_INTR1_INTR_STS1); if((rdata_grp & wr_val) != 0) pass else test_err++; raddr2 = MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8 + (i*4); write_reg(raddr2, 0x00110001); rdata = read_reg(raddr2); if(rdata == 0x100001) pass else test_err++; rdata_grp = read_reg(MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_INTR1_INTR_STS1); if(rdata_grp == 0x0) pass else test_err++; if GPIO0 defined: write_reg(MIZAR_LSS_SYSREG_RAW_STCR1, LSS_SYSREG_RAW_STCR1_GPIO0_INTR); GIC_ClearIRQ(87); if GPIO1 defined: write_reg(MIZAR_LSS_SYSREG_RAW_STCR1, LSS_SYSREG_RAW_STCR1_GPIO1_INTR); GIC_ClearIRQ(88); } else { test_err++; }","MIZAR_LSS_SYSREG_INTR_EN1, LSS_SYSREG_INTR_EN1_GPIO0_INTR, LSS_SYSREG_INTR_EN1_GPIO1_INTR, MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8, MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_INTR1_INTR_EN1, MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_INTR1_INTR_STS1, MIZAR_LSS_SYSREG_RAW_STCR1","- DIN check: if ((rdata & 0x1) != 0x0) then pass; else increment test_err.
- Raw interrupt check: if ((rdata & 0x2) != 0x0) then interrupt detected; else increment test_err.
- Group interrupt bit: read MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_INTR1_INTR_STS1; if ((rdata_grp & wr_val) != 0) then pass; else increment test_err.
- Per-pad clear: after writing 0x00110001 to per-pad register, readback must equal 0x100001; else increment test_err.
- Group clear: MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_INTR1_INTR_STS1 must read 0x0; else increment test_err.
- System raw clear: after writing the corresponding bit to MIZAR_LSS_SYSREG_RAW_STCR1, the bit must read as cleared." 
1,GPIO,dout,test_gpio_op_mode_all_pad_en,"Configure GPIO pads for output and verify pad output values for one and zero states. The test writes output values and checks pad status via a memory-mapped readback.",NA,NA,0xA0243ffc,0xA0243ffc,NA,"1) Configure GPIO_IO_CTRL_GROUP1, GPIO_IO_CTRL_GROUP2, GPIO_IO_CTRL_GROUP3, and gpio_io_ctrl_group4 to set pads in output mode.
2) Enable group interrupts in INTR1_INTR_EN1.
3) For each pad, write the per-pad register to drive output high, then read pad status via the memory-mapped interface.
4) For each pad, write the per-pad register to drive output low, then read pad status via the memory-mapped interface.
5) Record pass or fail based on pad status matching the driven output.","GPIO_IO_CTRL_GROUP1, GPIO_IO_CTRL_GROUP2, GPIO_IO_CTRL_GROUP3, gpio_io_ctrl_group4, INTR1_INTR_EN1, gp0_intr2_intr_en1","1) Output set to one → Pad status bit reads as one for the corresponding pad.
2) Output set to zero → Pad status bit reads as zero for the corresponding pad.",,"test_gpio_op_mode_all_pad_en","Enable IRQs (GIC_EnableIRQ 87/88 if defined). Set output mode for GPIOs 8–39 by writing 0x00FF00FF to MIZAR_GPIO_GPIO_IO_CTRL_GROUP1, MIZAR_GPIO_GPIO_IO_CTRL_GROUP2, MIZAR_GPIO_GPIO_IO_CTRL_GROUP3, and MIZAR_GPIO_GPIO_IO_CTRL_GROUP4; wait_on(10). Enable all group interrupts by writing 0xFFFFFFFF to MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_INTR1_INTR_EN1. For i from 0 to 31: write 0x00200000 to MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8 + (i*4) to drive output high; set gp0_flag_dout_one = 1; call check_for_pad_value(i). wait_on(20). Write 0x00000000 to MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8 + (i*4) to drive output low; set gp0_flag_dout_zero = 1; call check_for_pad_value(i). In check_for_pad_value: read rdata = read_reg(0xA0243ffc). If gp0_flag_dout_one == 1 then if (rdata & (1 << gpio_pad_num)) != 0 pass else print error and test_err++; clear gp0_flag_dout_one. If gp0_flag_dout_zero == 1 then if (rdata & (1 << gpio_pad_num)) == 0 pass else print error and test_err++; clear gp0_flag_dout_zero. Clear IRQ 87/88 if defined. Default_IRQHandler increments test_err if hit. finish(test_err) at end.",NA,"1) If GPIO0 defined: GIC_EnableIRQ(87); if GPIO1 defined: GIC_EnableIRQ(88). 2) Write 0x00FF00FF to MIZAR_GPIO_GPIO_IO_CTRL_GROUP1, MIZAR_GPIO_GPIO_IO_CTRL_GROUP2, MIZAR_GPIO_GPIO_IO_CTRL_GROUP3, and MIZAR_GPIO_GPIO_IO_CTRL_GROUP4. 3) wait_on(10). 4) Write 0xFFFFFFFF to MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_INTR1_INTR_EN1. 5) For i=0..31: write 0x00200000 to MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8 + (i*4); set gp0_flag_dout_one=1; call check_for_pad_value(i); wait_on(20); write 0x00000000 to MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8 + (i*4); set gp0_flag_dout_zero=1; call check_for_pad_value(i). 6) In check_for_pad_value: rdata = read_reg(0xA0243ffc); if gp0_flag_dout_one==1 then if((rdata & (1 << gpio_pad_num)) != 0) pass else print error and test_err++; set gp0_flag_dout_one=0; if gp0_flag_dout_zero==1 then if((rdata & (1 << gpio_pad_num)) == 0) pass else print error and test_err++; set gp0_flag_dout_zero=0; clear IRQ 87/88 if defined. 7) Default_IRQHandler prints error and increments test_err. 8) finish(test_err).","MIZAR_GPIO_GPIO_IO_CTRL_GROUP1, MIZAR_GPIO_GPIO_IO_CTRL_GROUP2, MIZAR_GPIO_GPIO_IO_CTRL_GROUP3, MIZAR_GPIO_GPIO_IO_CTRL_GROUP4, MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_INTR1_INTR_EN1, MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8","- For DOUT one: if (rdata & (1 << gpio_pad_num)) != 0 then pass else increment test_err.
- For DOUT zero: if (rdata & (1 << gpio_pad_num)) == 0 then pass else increment test_err."